      "id": "iincerc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Mahatma Gandhi (1869–1948)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Mahatma Gandhi (1869–1948) was a central figure in the Indian independence movement.",
        "Subhas Chandra Bose (1897–1945) led prominent nationalist efforts for Indian independence.",
        "Bhagat Singh (1907–1931) stands as one of the most prominent revolutionary figures.",
        "The 'Lal-Bal-Pal' triumvirate consisted of Lala Lajpat Rai (1865–1928), Bal Gangadhar Tilak (1856–1920), and Bipin Chandra Pal (1858–1932).",
        "Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel (1875–1950) and Jawaharlal Nehru (1889–1964) played critical roles in shaping modern India."
      ],
      "id": "6h1lw5o"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x1rjh4e",
      "content": "• Known as the 'Father of the Nation'."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nwyh8l4",
      "content": "• Leader of the Indian National Movement."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gcw08js",
      "content": "• Introduced Satyagraha and non-violent resistance."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h9v7q98",
      "content": "• Led Non-Cooperation (1920), Civil Disobedience (1930), Quit India (1942)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9nnhmqd",
      "content": "• Led the Dandi March in 1930."
    },
    {
      "id": "7bs46mu",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Subhas Chandra Bose (1897–1945)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dr2oof0",
      "content": "• Popularly known as Netaji."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tuxukl5",
      "content": "• Founded the Indian National Army (INA)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6t4it80",
      "content": "• Gave the slogan 'Give me blood and I will give you freedom'."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sop8rkq",
      "content": "• Formed the Azad Hind Government."
    },
    {
      "id": "ufjwmn3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Bhagat Singh (1907–1931)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uxpq3rt",
      "content": "• Famous revolutionary freedom fighter."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "n36iowv",
      "content": "• Involved in the Lahore Conspiracy Case."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wr8znsi",
      "content": "• Along with Batukeshwar Dutt threw bombs in the Central Legislative Assembly in 1929."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Chapter 14: Freedom Fighters of India",
      "id": "p6tk8hy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mc1rv60",
      "content": "• Executed by the British in 1931."
    },
    {
      "id": "oqlqe2j",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Rani Lakshmibai (1828–1858)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ycv2pn4",
      "content": "• Queen of Jhansi and leader in the Revolt of 1857."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "78a2xv2",
      "content": "• Fought bravely against British forces."
    },
    {
      "id": "s9pnmpb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Bal Gangadhar Tilak (1856–1920)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
